# WTDRV2Q.KEY - the modifier prefixes of the driver's mouse lines, run as
# WTDRV2 /MOUSE: SHIFT-, CTRL- and ALT- before an event, in any order and
# case, hold those keys down in Windows' key state, which the pads report
# after the buttons, and put MK_SHIFT and MK_CONTROL in wParam; the next
# mouse line sets them again, so one without them puts them up.
# TEST/mousechk.py replays it as it does WTDRV2M.
S INIT
M 70 SHIFT-DOWN AT 1 1
S SHIFT
M 70 ctrl-UP AT 2 2
S CTRL
M 70 Ctrl-Shift-DOWN AT 3 3
S BOTH
# no prefix: SHIFT and CTRL up again, the button still held
M 70 MOVE AT 4 4
S PLAIN
M 70 UP AT 4 4
# ALT has no MK_ bit
M 71 ALT-MOVE AT 5 5
S ALT
M 71 SHIFT-ALT-CTRL-MOVE AT 6 6
S ALL
# before a right button's event: the main window holds the mouse
M 70 SHIFT-RDOWN AT 7 7
S SHRDOWN
M 71 CTRL-RUP AT 8 8
S CTRLRUP
# before a double click on a class without CS_DBLCLKS, two deep
M 70.1 shift-DBL AT 1 2
S SHDBL
M 70.1 UP AT 1 2
S DBLUP
